5.1.text:
CHAPTER VI

INSTITUTION FOR THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR VICTIMS Article 13

(1) The Regional Government shall establish an Integrated Service Center for Women's and Children's Protection (P2TP2A) as an Institution for the Implementation, Prevention and Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence in an integrated manner.

(2) P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of elements: a. health;

b. law enforcement;

c. social and empowerment;

d. education and religious affairs;

e. Non-Governmental Organizations (NGOs); and

f. private sector.

(3) Further provisions regarding P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 8

Every victim has the right to receive:

a. protection;
b. information;
c. optimal service;
d. continuous treatment until the rehabilitation stage; and e. confidential treatment whether individual, group or institution whether government or non-government.

Article 20

(1) P2TP2A is obliged to report in writing the implementation of the provision of protection for Women and Children victims of violence to the Regent. (2) Report as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. administration;

b. finance;

c. services; and

d. performance.

(3) Submission of reports as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be carried out at least once every 3 (three) months.

